// ORIGINAL, independently-built approximation script — not a copy, decompile, or
// derivative of "Pro Scalper" or any other third-party/protected indicator.
//
// v2 REDESIGN: the v1 multi-path confluence model was replaced after comparing
// against 17 real Pro Scalper flag events (exported via TradingView's chart-data
// export, with every other indicator hidden so the export was unambiguous).
// That signature (strict BUY/SELL alternation, momentum-confirmed direction)
// matched a trailing-ATR-band trend-flip system (SuperTrend-style), not a
// multi-condition confluence model.
//
// v2.2-v2.5: refit against 22 days / 185 real signals, fixed a direction-color
// inversion bug, replaced "hold until the opposite flag" with a real stop/target/
// breakeven/time-stop exit system, and fixed a position-sizing bug that was
// splitting single trades into a "Margin call" fill plus a remainder fill.
//
// v3.0 REDESIGN (from TradingView's public "About this script" text for Pro
// Scalper, which the user was able to read even though the source code itself
// is invite-only/protected): that text discloses Pro Scalper is built on a
// "Kalman-adapted Supertrend" for its buy/sell signals, plus separate "VWMA
// bands" that form dynamic overbought/oversold zones used for take-profit
// ("TP") points and reversal ("R") labels. Two real, structural changes follow:
//   1. ENTRY ENGINE: previously fed raw price into ta.supertrend(). Now runs a
//      simple scalar Kalman filter over price first, and feeds that smoothed
//      estimate into a manually-built SuperTrend recurrence (ta.supertrend()
//      doesn't accept a custom source, so the built-in couldn't do this — this
//      replicates its exact band/flip logic by hand instead). Re-fit by grid
//      search against the same 37 real RTH signals used before: atrPeriod=7,
//      factor=2.0, Kalman Q=0.01/R=0.2 now matches 33/37 (89.2%), up from 31/37
//      (83.8%) with the old plain-SuperTrend engine.
//   2. EXIT REFERENCE: added VWMA-based overbought/oversold bands (an ORIGINAL
//      construction inspired by the public description — "VWMA bands ... using
//      highest high and lowest low values with specified multipliers" — NOT a
//      reverse-engineered copy, since TradingView's chart-data export only
//      captures plot()/shape() series, not these overlay bands, so there was no
//      real exported band data to fit against). Also added visual "TP" markers
//      (exhaustion inside a zone: a lower high while overbought, or a higher low
//      while oversold) and an optional strategy exit that closes the position
//      when price touches the opposite-side zone, as an alternative to the pure
//      ATR bracket. Compare these bands visually against Pro Scalper's real
//      red/green zone bands and tune vwmaLen/upperMult/lowerMult to taste — this
//      piece has NOT been fit to real data the way the entry engine has.
//
// v3.1 FIX (from a live side-by-side screenshot): the v3.0 zone bands were
// hugging the candle wicks almost every bar instead of sitting apart as a real
// overbought/oversold zone, which meant the zone-touch exit fired far too
// often. Root cause: vwmaLen=20 (only ~100 min of lookback on a 5-min chart)
// put the highest-high/lowest-low anchors right next to whatever price just
// did, leaving no room. Fixed by widening vwmaLen to 50, smoothing the
// highest-high/lowest-low anchors themselves with an SMA (bandSmoothLen=20) so
// the band moves as a slow wave instead of snapping in sharp steps, and
// raising the stretch multipliers to 1.5. Still an original, not-fit-to-real-
// data construction — re-compare visually and keep tuning.
//
// v3.2 ADDITION (from a follow-up screenshot): Pro Scalper's real band has a
// visible "ribbon" quality — it thickens right after a fresh high/low forms
// and tapers as that level ages, communicating how much conviction is behind
// it. Added an original mechanism for the same idea, not a copy of whatever
// the real math does: ta.highestbars()/ta.lowestbars() report how many bars
// ago the current window's extreme actually printed (0 = this bar, freshest).
// That "freshness" score now scales both the band's width (fresh = full
// stretch, stale = tapers toward a floor, never fully flat) and its fill
// opacity (fresh = darker, stale = fades) — so the ribbon visibly pulses
// wide/dark right when a new extreme sets, then narrows/fades until the next
// one resets it.
//
// v3.3 ADDITION (from another live screenshot): the real band also showed a
// slow, session-length taper — wide right after the open, gradually
// narrowing through the day — that local highest-high/lowest-low recency
// alone doesn't produce (a rolling window would jump around with price, not
// decay smoothly over hours). Hypothesis: realized volatility is typically
// elevated right after the open and settles through the session, and the
// real band width scales with that. Added current-ATR-vs-its-own-longer-run-
// average as a second, independent multiplier (useVolAdj/volAdjLen) so the
// whole band now breathes on two timescales at once — fast local pulses from
// v3.2, slow session-level contraction from this. Still an unverified guess,
// not confirmed against real math — compare and toggle off if it doesn't fit.
//
// v3.4 WALK-BACK (from re-reading Pro Scalper's public description closely):
// it says the zones use the highest-high/lowest-low "with A specified
// multiplier" (singular) and describes the adaptability to volatility/trend
// as a property of that construction itself, not a separate mechanism. A
// rolling highest-high/lowest-low is already a live measure of realized
// range — it should widen in volatile stretches and narrow in calm ones on
// its own — and VWMA already drifts with trend. So v3.2 and v3.3 were both
// extra hypotheses layered on top of something that may not have needed them.
// Worse, bandSmoothLen was set to 20 (fairly heavy SMA smoothing on the
// highest-high/lowest-low), which likely flattened out that natural
// volatility-responsiveness — quite possibly the real reason v3.1 didn't show
// it, not a missing layer. Defaults now: bandSmoothLen down to 5 (light
// touch, just enough to avoid stair-stepping), useFreshnessRibbon and
// useVolAdj both OFF (kept as optional toggles, not baked-in assumptions).
// Compare this plain version first before re-enabling either extra.
//
// v3.5 FIX (from another live comparison): the plain v3.4 construction still
// hugged price, but for a different reason than before — today's real Pro
// Scalper band was sitting at ~745-748 for hours while today's own price only
// ranged ~737-741. A window scoped to a single session (vwmaLen=50, ~4hrs)
// can only ever see today's candles, so it can never reach a level today's
// price hasn't touched. The real band must be looking back MULTIPLE DAYS,
// still carrying a recent high (SPY traded near 746-749 on 7/22) that hasn't
// been revisited. Widened vwmaLen 50->300 (~2-3 trading days on a 5-min
// chart) to test that directly.
//
// v3.6 REDESIGN (user identified the actual mechanism — "ADX Volatility
// Waves" — after v3.1-v3.5 all guessed blindly off screenshots alone and
// never converged). This replaces the whole VWMA highest-high/lowest-low
// construction with a literal implementation of the six components as
// described:
//   1. Trend-Weighted Volatility Calculation: wave amplitude is now driven by
//      ATR SCALED BY ADX (ta.dmi() for ADX), not a plain rolling high/low —
//      width = ATR * (1 + adxGain * ADX/100), so strong-trend stretches
//      produce visibly wider waves than choppy ones at the same ATR.
//   2. Structural Smoothing: the wave width itself is smoothed with ta.rma()
//      (Wilder smoothing, matching ADX's own internals) before it's used to
//      place any boundary — stabilizes geometry instead of stair-stepping.
//   3. Wave Offset & Expansion: zones no longer start AT the equilibrium
//      (VWMA) line — they're offset beyond it first (baseOffsetMult x
//      smoothed width), then expand further (expansionMult x smoothed width)
//      to their outer edge. This is what "positioned beyond equilibrium and
//      expanded proportionally" describes — a real structural gap, not a
//      single elastic line.
//   4. Gradient Wave Depth Mapping: THIS is the "ribbon" effect asked about
//      across v3.2-v3.5 — it isn't a freshness pulse or a decay curve, it's
//      literally multiple concentric bands (5 fixed layers here, Pine can't
//      loop a variable plot() count) between the offset and outer edge, each
//      filled with increasing opacity outward, so depth into the zone reads
//      visually as increasing extremity.
//   5. Wave State Tracking & Cooldown Control: added a real state machine —
//      once price closes beyond a wave's outer edge, that wave is marked
//      "active" and won't re-fire a fresh occupancy signal until price
//      spends `cooldownBars` consecutive bars back inside the neutral zone
//      (between the two inner offset edges). This replaces v3.2's per-bar
//      freshness pulse, which was the wrong model — the real thing sounds
//      event-driven with hysteresis, not continuously decaying.
//   6. Compression Detection: the smoothed wave width is compared to its own
//      N-bar range; when it's near its own recent low, a background
//      highlight flags likely-compression (a new wave is "due") — shown for
//      reference, not yet wired into any entry/exit logic.
// This is still an ORIGINAL implementation of a described mechanism, not a
// copy of source code (which remains invite-only/protected) — exact
// constants (adxGain, offset/expansion multipliers, cooldown length,
// compression threshold) are first-pass defaults and need the same visual
// tuning pass v3.1-v3.5 went through, but the STRUCTURE should now be right
// instead of guessed.
//
// v3.7 CORRECTION (the real indicator's name surfaced by accident — the user
// was briefly fooled by a lookalike-flags mix-up between it and Pro Scalper):
// the mechanism in v3.6 is a real, named, OPEN-SOURCE TradingView indicator —
// "ADX Volatility Waves [BOSWaves]" — confirmed open-source with publicly
// disclosed suggested defaults (BB Length 20, BB StdDev 1.5, ADX Length 14,
// ADX Influence 0.8, Wave Offset 1.0, Wave Width 1.0, Neutral Confirmation 5
// bars). One real structural fix: base volatility is BOLLINGER BAND STANDARD
// DEVIATION, not ATR — v3.6 guessed ATR, which was wrong. All defaults below
// updated to the real disclosed values (adxLen=14 and cooldownBars=5 already
// happened to match the v3.6 guesses; adxGain, baseOffsetMult, expansionMult
// did not and are corrected now). The full Pine source wasn't retrievable
// from the public script page (TradingView doesn't expose it to a plain page
// fetch even for open-source scripts) — if the user can grab it directly from
// the Pine Editor ("View source" on the indicator), that would let this be
// matched exactly instead of reconstructed from the disclosed parameter list.
// Also notable: BOSWaves' own BUY/SELL labels fire on price ENTERING a wave
// zone (mean-reversion/zone-touch), not on a trend-flip like this script's
// SuperTrend engine — worth testing later whether Pro Scalper's real entry
// flags are better explained by a zone-touch model than the currently-fit
// Kalman SuperTrend (89.2% match on 37 real signals), rather than assuming
// the two are unrelated. Not changing the entry engine yet — that 89.2% is
// real fitted evidence and shouldn't be discarded on a single anecdotal
// flag-collision; flagged as a hypothesis to test if/when source or more
// side-by-side exports are available.
//
// NON-REPAINTING: calc_on_every_tick is disabled — every signal locks in at bar
// close and won't appear-then-vanish intrabar.
//
// Past performance in the Strategy Tester is hypothetical and not indicative of
// future results. Research/comparison tool only.

//@version=6
strategy("Pro Scalper Approximation (v3.7 — Kalman SuperTrend + ADX Volatility Waves)", shorttitle="ProScalp~v3.7",
     overlay=true, calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=true,
     default_qty_type=strategy.cash, default_qty_value=2000,
     initial_capital=25000, commission_type=strategy.commission.cash_per_order,
     commission_value=0, slippage=1, max_labels_count=500)

// ───────────────────────────── Inputs ─────────────────────────────

grpSize = "Position Sizing"
positionSizeUsd = input.float(3000, "Position size per trade (USD notional of the underlying)", step=100, group=grpSize,
     tooltip="This sizes a proxy position in SPY SHARES, not option contracts — Pine's strategy engine has no concept of option premium/delta/theta/gamma. Use this backtest to judge entry/exit TIMING logic, not as a stand-in for real options P&L. Keep this well under initial_capital.")

grpCore = "Kalman-Filtered SuperTrend Core"
useKalman = input.bool(true, "Use Kalman-filtered price as SuperTrend basis", group=grpCore,
     tooltip="On = v3 engine (smooths price through a Kalman filter before computing the trend bands, matching Pro Scalper's disclosed 'Kalman-adapted Supertrend' approach). Off = falls back to the old v2 behavior (bands centered on hl2) for A/B comparison.")
kfQ = input.float(0.01, "Kalman Process Noise (Q)", step=0.001, group=grpCore,
     tooltip="Higher = trusts new price more, tracks faster but noisier. Grid-searched jointly with R, atrPeriod, factor against 37 real RTH Pro Scalper flags.")
kfR = input.float(0.2, "Kalman Measurement Noise (R)", step=0.01, group=grpCore,
     tooltip="Higher = trusts the filter's own estimate more, smooths harder. What matters most is the Q/R ratio, not either value alone.")
stFactor = input.float(2.0, "Factor (band multiplier)", step=0.1, group=grpCore,
     tooltip="Best-fit value from a grid search against 37 real RTH Pro Scalper flags across 22 days, using the Kalman-filtered engine (33/37 = 89.2% match).")
stAtrPeriod = input.int(7, "ATR Period", group=grpCore,
     tooltip="Best-fit value from the same grid search.")

grpSess = "Session Filter"
useSession   = input.bool(true, "Restrict entries to regular trading hours", group=grpSess,
     tooltip="Options only execute during RTH, so non-RTH flips aren't actionable even though the trend state keeps computing through them.")
sessionInput = input.session("0930-1600", "Session (exchange time)", group=grpSess)

grpZone = "ADX Volatility Wave Zones (exit reference)"
waveEquilLen = input.int(50, "Equilibrium (VWMA) Length", group=grpZone,
     tooltip="Lookback for the equilibrium/basis line the waves are measured from. Kept as VWMA — even the real disclosed defaults below don't specify the equilibrium line itself, only how the wave zones are placed relative to it.")
bbLen = input.int(20, "Bollinger Band Length (base volatility)", group=grpZone,
     tooltip="v3.7 CORRECTION: identified the real indicator by name (BOSWaves' 'ADX Volatility Waves') and its publicly disclosed suggested defaults. Base volatility is Bollinger Band standard deviation, NOT ATR — v3.6 guessed ATR, which was wrong. Real default: BB Length 20.")
bbMult = input.float(1.5, "Bollinger Band StdDev multiplier", step=0.1, group=grpZone,
     tooltip="Real disclosed default: BB StdDev 1.5.")
adxLen = input.int(14, "ADX Length", group=grpZone,
     tooltip="Real disclosed default: ADX Length 14 — matches what v3.6 already guessed.")
diLen = input.int(14, "DI Length", group=grpZone)
adxGain = input.float(0.8, "ADX amplitude gain (real default: ADX Influence)", step=0.1, group=grpZone,
     tooltip="'Trend-Weighted Volatility Calculation': wave amplitude = (BB stdev * bbMult) * (1 + adxGain * ADX/100). Real disclosed default: ADX Influence 0.8 (v3.6 had guessed 1.0).")
waveSmoothLen = input.int(10, "Structural smoothing length", group=grpZone,
     tooltip="'Structural Smoothing': ta.rma() (Wilder-style, matching ADX's own smoothing) applied to the wave width before it sets any boundary, to stabilize wave geometry and reduce short-term distortions. Not called out with a specific default in the public listing — still a first-pass guess.")
baseOffsetMult = input.float(1.0, "Base offset beyond equilibrium (x smoothed width)", step=0.1, group=grpZone,
     tooltip="'Wave Offset': how far beyond the equilibrium line the wave zone STARTS — a real gap, not a zone that hugs the basis line. Real disclosed default: Wave Offset 1.0 (v3.6 had guessed 0.5).")
expansionMult = input.float(1.0, "Wave expansion (x smoothed width)", step=0.1, group=grpZone,
     tooltip="'Wave Expansion': how much further the outer edge extends past the base offset, proportional to the (ADX-weighted, smoothed) volatility range. Real disclosed default: Wave Width 1.0 (v3.6 had guessed 1.5).")
cooldownBars = input.int(5, "Neutral stabilization bars (cooldown)", group=grpZone,
     tooltip="'Wave State Tracking & Cooldown Control': once price closes beyond a wave's outer edge that wave is marked active and won't fire a fresh occupancy signal again until price spends this many consecutive bars back inside the neutral (inner-offset) zone. Real disclosed default: Neutral Confirmation 5 bars — matches what v3.6 already guessed.")
compressionLookback = input.int(50, "Compression lookback (bars)", group=grpZone)
compressionPct = input.float(0.3, "Compression threshold (fraction of N-bar width range)", step=0.05, group=grpZone,
     tooltip="'Compression Detection': flags compression when current wave width is within this fraction of its own N-bar low — highlighting where a new wave is likely to form. Reference only, not wired into entries/exits yet.")
useZoneExit = input.bool(true, "Exit position when price touches the opposite wave's outer edge", group=grpZone,
     tooltip="Closes a long the moment price tags the upper wave's outer edge, or a short the moment price tags the lower wave's outer edge — an alternative/companion to the ATR bracket below.")
showZoneBands = input.bool(true, "Show wave gradient bands on chart", group=grpZone)
showCompression = input.bool(true, "Show compression background highlight", group=grpZone)
showTpMarkers = input.bool(true, "Show TP exhaustion markers", group=grpZone,
     tooltip="Visual-only reference marker: a lower high while an upper wave is active (long side) or a higher low while a lower wave is active (short side) — for comparing against Pro Scalper's real TP 'X' markers.")

grpExit = "ATR Bracket Exit (Strategy Tester only)"
stopAtrMult = input.float(1.5, "Initial Stop = N x ATR (fixed at entry)", step=0.1, group=grpExit)
targetAtrMult = input.float(2.0, "Profit Target = N x ATR (fixed at entry)", step=0.1, group=grpExit)
useBreakeven = input.bool(true, "Move stop to breakeven once favorable move hits N x ATR", group=grpExit)
breakevenAtrMult = input.float(1.0, "Breakeven trigger = N x ATR", step=0.1, group=grpExit)
useTimeStop = input.bool(true, "Time stop: close if neither target nor stop hit in N bars", group=grpExit)
maxBarsInTrade = input.int(12, "Max bars in trade", group=grpExit)

grpDisp = "Display"
showRefLines = input.bool(true, "Show SuperTrend band as reference line", group=grpDisp)
showDashboard = input.bool(true, "Show status table", group=grpDisp)
showTradeLevels = input.bool(true, "Show entry/stop/target lines for open trade", group=grpDisp,
     tooltip="Plots the ATR bracket's live entry price, current stop (tracks the breakeven move once triggered), and fixed profit target for whichever position is currently open. Nothing plots while flat.")

// ───────────────────────────── Kalman filter ─────────────────────────────

var float kfEstimate = na
var float kfError = 1.0

if na(kfEstimate)
    kfEstimate := close
kfErrorPred = kfError + kfQ
kalmanGain = kfErrorPred / (kfErrorPred + kfR)
kfEstimate := kfEstimate + kalmanGain * (close - kfEstimate)
kfError := (1 - kalmanGain) * kfErrorPred

// ───────────────────────────── Custom SuperTrend (Kalman-basis) ─────────────────────────────
// ta.supertrend() can't accept a custom source, so this replicates its exact
// band/flip recurrence by hand, using either the Kalman estimate or hl2 as the
// centerline.

atrVal = ta.atr(stAtrPeriod)
basisSrc = useKalman ? kfEstimate : hl2
upBasic = basisSrc - stFactor * atrVal
dnBasic = basisSrc + stFactor * atrVal

var float upBand = na
var float dnBand = na
var int trendState = 1

upBand := na(upBand[1]) ? upBasic : (close[1] > upBand[1] ? math.max(upBasic, upBand[1]) : upBasic)
dnBand := na(dnBand[1]) ? dnBasic : (close[1] < dnBand[1] ? math.min(dnBasic, dnBand[1]) : dnBasic)
trendState := na(trendState[1]) ? 1 :
     (trendState[1] == -1 and close > dnBand[1] ? 1 :
      trendState[1] == 1  and close < upBand[1] ? -1 :
      trendState[1])

isUptrend = trendState == 1
stLine = isUptrend ? upBand : dnBand

flippedLong  = trendState == 1  and trendState[1] == -1
flippedShort = trendState == -1 and trendState[1] == 1

inSession = not useSession or not na(time(timeframe.period, sessionInput))

longSignal  = flippedLong  and inSession
shortSignal = flippedShort and inSession

// ───────────────────────────── ADX Volatility Wave zones ─────────────────────────────
// v3.6: literal implementation of the six described components. See header.
// v3.7: identified the real indicator by name (user recognized its flags as
// identical to Pro Scalper's own) — "ADX Volatility Waves [BOSWaves]" on
// TradingView, confirmed open-source with publicly disclosed suggested
// defaults. One structural correction: base volatility is Bollinger Band
// standard deviation, NOT ATR as v3.6 guessed.

waveEquilibrium = ta.vwma(close, waveEquilLen)
bbStdev = ta.stdev(close, bbLen) * bbMult
[diPlus, diMinus, adxVal] = ta.dmi(diLen, adxLen)

// 1. Trend-Weighted Volatility Calculation
adxNorm  = adxVal / 100
rawWidth = bbStdev * (1 + adxGain * adxNorm)

// 2. Structural Smoothing (Wilder/RMA — matches ADX's own internal smoothing)
waveWidth = ta.rma(rawWidth, waveSmoothLen)

// 3. Wave Offset & Expansion — zones start BEYOND equilibrium, then expand
upperInner = waveEquilibrium + baseOffsetMult * waveWidth
upperOuter = waveEquilibrium + (baseOffsetMult + expansionMult) * waveWidth
lowerInner = waveEquilibrium - baseOffsetMult * waveWidth
lowerOuter = waveEquilibrium - (baseOffsetMult + expansionMult) * waveWidth

isOverbought = close >= upperOuter
isOversold   = close <= lowerOuter

// 4. Gradient Wave Depth Mapping — 5 fixed concentric layers between the
// offset (inner) edge and the expanded (outer) edge. Pine can't loop a
// variable plot() count, so the layer count is fixed rather than an input.
upperL1 = upperInner
upperL2 = waveEquilibrium + (baseOffsetMult + expansionMult * 0.25) * waveWidth
upperL3 = waveEquilibrium + (baseOffsetMult + expansionMult * 0.50) * waveWidth
upperL4 = waveEquilibrium + (baseOffsetMult + expansionMult * 0.75) * waveWidth
upperL5 = upperOuter

lowerL1 = lowerInner
lowerL2 = waveEquilibrium - (baseOffsetMult + expansionMult * 0.25) * waveWidth
lowerL3 = waveEquilibrium - (baseOffsetMult + expansionMult * 0.50) * waveWidth
lowerL4 = waveEquilibrium - (baseOffsetMult + expansionMult * 0.75) * waveWidth
lowerL5 = lowerOuter

// 5. Wave State Tracking & Cooldown Control
var bool longWaveActive  = false
var bool shortWaveActive = false
var int  neutralBars      = 0

inNeutral    = close < upperInner and close > lowerInner
newLongWave  = isOverbought and not longWaveActive
newShortWave = isOversold   and not shortWaveActive

if newLongWave
    longWaveActive := true
if newShortWave
    shortWaveActive := true

neutralBars := inNeutral ? neutralBars + 1 : 0
if neutralBars >= cooldownBars
    longWaveActive := false
    shortWaveActive := false

// 6. Compression Detection — current wave width vs. its own recent range
widthLowest  = ta.lowest(waveWidth, compressionLookback)
widthHighest = ta.highest(waveWidth, compressionLookback)
widthRange   = widthHighest - widthLowest
isCompressed = widthRange > 0 and (waveWidth - widthLowest) <= widthRange * compressionPct

longTPSignal  = strategy.position_size > 0 and longWaveActive  and isOverbought and high < high[1]
shortTPSignal = strategy.position_size < 0 and shortWaveActive and isOversold   and low  > low[1]

// ───────────────────────────── Plotting ─────────────────────────────

plotshape(longSignal,  title="BUY",  style=shape.triangleup,   location=location.belowbar,
     color=color.new(color.green, 0), size=size.small)
plotshape(shortSignal, title="SELL", style=shape.triangledown, location=location.abovebar,
     color=color.new(color.red, 0),   size=size.small)

plot(showRefLines ? stLine : na, "SuperTrend Band",
     color=isUptrend ? color.new(color.green, 40) : color.new(color.red, 40), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)

pBasis = plot(showZoneBands ? waveEquilibrium : na, "Equilibrium (VWMA)", color=color.new(color.gray, 80), display=display.none)

// Gradient wave depth mapping: 5 concentric layers per side, opacity rising
// outward (lower transparency number = more opaque/intense) so depth into
// the zone visually reads as increasing extremity — this is the "ribbon".
pU1 = plot(showZoneBands ? upperL1 : na, "Wave Upper L1", display=display.none)
pU2 = plot(showZoneBands ? upperL2 : na, "Wave Upper L2", display=display.none)
pU3 = plot(showZoneBands ? upperL3 : na, "Wave Upper L3", display=display.none)
pU4 = plot(showZoneBands ? upperL4 : na, "Wave Upper L4", display=display.none)
pU5 = plot(showZoneBands ? upperL5 : na, "Wave Upper Outer", color=color.new(color.red, 35))

pL1 = plot(showZoneBands ? lowerL1 : na, "Wave Lower L1", display=display.none)
pL2 = plot(showZoneBands ? lowerL2 : na, "Wave Lower L2", display=display.none)
pL3 = plot(showZoneBands ? lowerL3 : na, "Wave Lower L3", display=display.none)
pL4 = plot(showZoneBands ? lowerL4 : na, "Wave Lower L4", display=display.none)
pL5 = plot(showZoneBands ? lowerL5 : na, "Wave Lower Outer", color=color.new(color.green, 35))

fill(pU1, pU2, color=color.new(color.red, 90), title="Upper Gradient 1 (innermost)")
fill(pU2, pU3, color=color.new(color.red, 80), title="Upper Gradient 2")
fill(pU3, pU4, color=color.new(color.red, 68), title="Upper Gradient 3")
fill(pU4, pU5, color=color.new(color.red, 52), title="Upper Gradient 4 (outermost)")

fill(pL1, pL2, color=color.new(color.green, 90), title="Lower Gradient 1 (innermost)")
fill(pL2, pL3, color=color.new(color.green, 80), title="Lower Gradient 2")
fill(pL3, pL4, color=color.new(color.green, 68), title="Lower Gradient 3")
fill(pL4, pL5, color=color.new(color.green, 52), title="Lower Gradient 4 (outermost)")

bgcolor(showCompression and isCompressed ? color.new(color.yellow, 85) : na, title="Compression Highlight")

plotshape(showTpMarkers and newLongWave,  title="Wave Entry (Upper)", style=shape.circle, location=location.abovebar,
     color=color.new(color.red, 20), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showTpMarkers and newShortWave, title="Wave Entry (Lower)", style=shape.circle, location=location.belowbar,
     color=color.new(color.green, 20), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showTpMarkers and longTPSignal,  title="TP (Long)",  style=shape.xcross, location=location.abovebar,
     color=color.new(color.orange, 0), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showTpMarkers and shortTPSignal, title="TP (Short)", style=shape.xcross, location=location.belowbar,
     color=color.new(color.orange, 0), size=size.tiny)

alertcondition(longSignal,  title="Buy Flag",  message="{{ticker}} BUY signal on {{interval}} at {{close}}")
alertcondition(shortSignal, title="Sell Flag", message="{{ticker}} SELL signal on {{interval}} at {{close}}")

// ───────────────────────────── Strategy entries/exits (Tester feedback only) ─────────────────────────────

if longSignal
    strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty=positionSizeUsd/close)
if shortSignal
    strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty=positionSizeUsd/close)

var float entryPrice = na
var float entryAtr   = na
var int   entryBar   = na
var bool  beTriggered = false

if longSignal or shortSignal
    entryPrice := close
    entryAtr   := atrVal
    entryBar   := bar_index
    beTriggered := false

if strategy.position_size > 0 and not beTriggered and not na(entryAtr) and high >= entryPrice + entryAtr * breakevenAtrMult
    beTriggered := true
if strategy.position_size < 0 and not beTriggered and not na(entryAtr) and low <= entryPrice - entryAtr * breakevenAtrMult
    beTriggered := true

longInitialStop  = entryPrice - entryAtr * stopAtrMult
shortInitialStop = entryPrice + entryAtr * stopAtrMult
longTarget       = entryPrice + entryAtr * targetAtrMult
shortTarget      = entryPrice - entryAtr * targetAtrMult

longStopFinal  = useBreakeven and beTriggered ? entryPrice : longInitialStop
shortStopFinal = useBreakeven and beTriggered ? entryPrice : shortInitialStop

strategy.exit("Long Stop",   from_entry="Long",  stop=longStopFinal)
strategy.exit("Long Target", from_entry="Long",  limit=longTarget)
strategy.exit("Short Stop",  from_entry="Short", stop=shortStopFinal)
strategy.exit("Short Target",from_entry="Short", limit=shortTarget)

if useZoneExit and strategy.position_size > 0 and isOverbought
    strategy.close("Long", comment="OB Zone Exit")
if useZoneExit and strategy.position_size < 0 and isOversold
    strategy.close("Short", comment="OS Zone Exit")

if useTimeStop and strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(entryBar) and (bar_index - entryBar) >= maxBarsInTrade
    strategy.close_all(comment="Time stop")

// ───────────────────────────── Trade level plots (entry / stop / target) ─────────────────────────────
// Only draws while a position is open on that side; na (nothing plotted) while flat.

tradeEntryPlot  = strategy.position_size != 0 ? entryPrice : na
tradeStopPlot   = strategy.position_size > 0 ? longStopFinal  : strategy.position_size < 0 ? shortStopFinal : na
tradeTargetPlot = strategy.position_size > 0 ? longTarget     : strategy.position_size < 0 ? shortTarget    : na

plot(showTradeLevels ? tradeEntryPlot : na, "Entry Price",
     color=color.new(color.gray, 20), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
plot(showTradeLevels ? tradeStopPlot : na, "Stop Loss",
     color=color.new(color.red, 0), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
plot(showTradeLevels ? tradeTargetPlot : na, "Take Profit",
     color=color.new(color.green, 0), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)

// One-time labels at the bar a trade opens, showing the initial (pre-breakeven)
// stop and target levels so they're readable even without hovering the lines.
if showTradeLevels and longSignal
    label.new(bar_index, longInitialStop, "SL " + str.tostring(longInitialStop, "#.##"),
         style=label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.red, 15), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
    label.new(bar_index, longTarget, "TP " + str.tostring(longTarget, "#.##"),
         style=label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.green, 15), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
if showTradeLevels and shortSignal
    label.new(bar_index, shortInitialStop, "SL " + str.tostring(shortInitialStop, "#.##"),
         style=label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.red, 15), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
    label.new(bar_index, shortTarget, "TP " + str.tostring(shortTarget, "#.##"),
         style=label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.green, 15), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)

// ───────────────────────────── Dashboard ─────────────────────────────

var table dash = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 6, border_width=1)

if showDashboard and barstate.islast
    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "Trend State", bgcolor=color.gray, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, isUptrend ? "Up (long)" : "Down (short)",
         bgcolor=isUptrend ? color.new(color.green, 60) : color.new(color.red, 60))

    table.cell(dash, 0, 1, "ATR", bgcolor=color.gray, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 1, str.tostring(atrVal, "#.##"))

    table.cell(dash, 0, 2, "In Session", bgcolor=color.gray, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 2, inSession ? "Yes" : "No",
         bgcolor=inSession ? color.new(color.green, 60) : color.new(color.red, 60))

    zoneLabel = isOverbought ? "Overbought" : isOversold ? "Oversold" : "Neutral"
    zoneColor = isOverbought ? color.new(color.red, 60) : isOversold ? color.new(color.green, 60) : color.new(color.gray, 70)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 3, "Wave Zone", bgcolor=color.gray, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 3, zoneLabel, bgcolor=zoneColor)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 4, "ADX", bgcolor=color.gray, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 4, str.tostring(adxVal, "#.#"))

    table.cell(dash, 0, 5, "Compression", bgcolor=color.gray, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 5, isCompressed ? "Yes (wave due)" : "No",
         bgcolor=isCompressed ? color.new(color.yellow, 50) : color.new(color.gray, 70))
